---
import JournalLayout from '../layouts/JournalLayout.astro';

const lang = 'en';
---

<JournalLayout
  title="About the Journal"
  description="About Ayamatma: A Journal of Vedantic Studies."
  lang={lang}
>
  <section class="section stack">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="section-title">About the Journal</h1>
    <p class="muted">
      Ayamatma is a journal for disciplined Vedāntic inquiry and serious public philosophy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Ayamatma: A Journal of Vedantic Studies</strong> is an independent open-access
        online journal devoted to Vedānta, Hindu philosophy, Sanskrit textual interpretation,
        Dharma, consciousness, and the dialogue between traditional knowledge and modern inquiry.
      </p>

      <p>
        The journal is not designed as a sectarian platform, a casual blog, or a journalistic magazine
        wearing scholarly dress. Its basic commitment is argument under discipline: terms must be defined,
        sources must be traceable, translations must be honest about interpretive choices, and claims must
        be separated from speculation.
      </p>

      <p>
        The journal welcomes work that is rooted in Hindu and Vedāntic traditions while remaining clear,
        critical, and intelligible to readers outside a single lineage. It also welcomes careful engagement
        with science, philosophy of mind, linguistics, ethics, history, and comparative thought, provided the
        engagement does not flatten either side into easy analogy.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial identity</h2>
      <p>
        Editor-in-Chief: <strong>Kiran Boggavarapu</strong>, Professor of Chemistry &amp; Physics,
        McNeese State University.
      </p>
      <p>
        Publisher: <strong>Ayamatma Press</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Status</h2>
      <p>
        The journal infrastructure is under development. ISSN registration and article-level DOIs are planned
        after the first issue and stable article landing pages are in place. No ISSN, DOI, indexing status,
        impact factor, or completed peer-review status is claimed unless explicitly displayed on a final
        published article page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</JournalLayout>
